---
title: "El curioso incidente de la latencia causado por el FW"
date: 2023-02-29T09:00:00+01:00
draft: false
---

Hoy he tenido un caso que me ha dejado trastocado.

Todo empieza por un incidente en el que el cliente afirma que desde on-prem hasta una máquina en AZURE, usando un paping 
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paping (que es un TCP ping), estaba perdiendo paquetes y dando latencias inconsistentes.

Después de tirar mucho del hilo, veo que todo el tráfico desde la máquina de destino a on-prem atraviesa un AZFW
https://azuresupportcenter.msftcloudes.com/resourceexplorerv2/resource/%2Fsubscriptions%2F5f82d5c3-ea71-45f3-826a-4dbbcf6bf5e0%2FresourceGroups%2Fprod-mgmt-hub-vnet-eastus2-01%2Fproviders%2Fmicrosoft.network%2Fazurefirewalls%2Fprod-phub-eastus2-fw-01?srId=2402280040013726

Y en el dashboard del AZFW Diagnostics --> Performance Metrics

En la sección CPU total active, se ve un incremento brutal


En los Dataplane metrics, se ve un cambio de versión

https://portal.microsoftgeneva.com/s/3D4BE8D5?overrides=%5b%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=%27ResourceId%27%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22/subscriptions/5f82d5c3-ea71-45f3-826a-4dbbcf6bf5e0/resourceGroups/prod-mgmt-hub-vnet-eastus2-01/providers/Microsoft.Network/azureFirewalls/prod-phub-eastus2-fw-01%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=%27Hostname%27%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=%27Region%27%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=\%22tenant\%22%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22/subscriptions/5f82d5c3-ea71-45f3-826a-4dbbcf6bf5e0/resourceGroups/prod-mgmt-hub-vnet-eastus2-01/providers/Microsoft.Network/azureFirewalls/prod-phub-eastus2-fw-01%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bcomparand=\%22Tenant\%22%5d%22,%22key%22:%22values%22,%22replacement%22:%22/subscriptions/5f82d5c3-ea71-45f3-826a-4dbbcf6bf5e0/resourceGroups/prod-mgmt-hub-vnet-eastus2-01/providers/Microsoft.Network/azureFirewalls/prod-phub-eastus2-fw-01%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=%27rid%27%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22/subscriptions/5f82d5c3-ea71-45f3-826a-4dbbcf6bf5e0/resourceGroups/prod-mgmt-hub-vnet-eastus2-01/providers/Microsoft.Network/azureFirewalls/prod-phub-eastus2-fw-01%22%7d,%7b%22query%22:%22//*%5bid=%27GatewayId%27%5d%22,%22key%22:%22value%22,%22replacement%22:%22%22%7d%5d%20

En el Num of healthy instances per Gateway Version (Based on metric FirewallHealth)

Cambia de la versión 0.3.11 to 0.3.12


Se puede hacer desde un 

Brooklyn > Azure Firewall Operations > Get Azure Firewall
https://portal-east.microsoftgeneva.com/?page=actions&acisEndpoint=Public&managementOpen=false&automatedTestsReportOpen=false&bakingDetailsOpen=false&tab=Extensions&acisRolloutEndpoint=Public&selectedNodeType=3&extension=Brooklyn&group=Azure%20Firewall%20Operations&operationId=getazurefirewall&operationName=Get%20Azure%20Firewall&inputMode=single&params={"resource_id":"","smegatewaymanagerregion":"NONE"}&actionEndpoint=Brooklyn%20-%20Prod&genevatraceguid=23770382-81e0-47dc-b2eb-bcf36691aaef


